JIRA ID : ALMIOPEN-2841

## Motivation

`miopen_gtest_quick_suite` reports failures on gfx1250. One of them is
`Smoke/CPU_UnitTestConvSolverConvDepthwiseFwd2DDevApplicability_FP16.ConvDepthwiseFwd2D/0`.
This is a device-applicability test, and its expected device list did
not include gfx1250. The CK depthwise forward instances are already
built for gfx1250, so `ConvDepthwiseFwd2D` is applicable there and the
test expectation was stale.

## Technical Details

In `GetTestParams` in
`projects/miopen/test/gtest/unit_conv_solver_ConvCkGroupedConvFwd.cpp`,
`Gpu::gfx125X` is added to `supportedDevices`.

- `src/ck_impl/CMakeLists.txt` lists `gfx1250` in `_CK_SUPPORTED_ARCHS`
and builds the depthwise forward instances for it.
- `ConvDepthwiseFwd2D::IsApplicable` has no wave-size or arch gate, so
it applies on gfx1250 once the CK library is loaded.
- `ConvDepthwiseBwdData2D` is intentionally unchanged. It rejects
devices whose wavefront width is not 64, and gfx1250 is wave32.

`GetTestParams` is shared with the bf16 GPU tests in the same file, so
those also now expect gfx1250 to be supported.

This PR only addresses the depthwise group from ALMIOPEN-2841. The
GemmFwdRest, GemmBwdRest and GemmWrwUniversal failures listed in the
ticket are not covered here.

## Risk Assessment

**Risk Level: 🟢 Low**

### Impacted Components

- MIOpen gtest `unit_conv_solver_ConvCkGroupedConvFwd` (test code only).

### Potential Side Effects

None for library behavior; only a test expectation changes. On gfx1250
builds where the CK depthwise instances are not built, the test would
now expect applicability and fail.

### Mitigation Steps

The change is one line in a test and is trivially revertible.

## Test Plan

Run on a gfx1250 target:

```
miopen_gtest --gtest_filter='*ConvDepthwiseFwd2D*'
```

Also run the same filter on gfx942 and gfx950 to confirm no change
there.

## Test Result

Not yet run in this session. Pending verification on gfx1250 (and
gfx942/gfx950 for regressions).

